From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:02:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] sdk: support typed runtime values and bulk query
 collection

Use the runtime capability boundary for bulk collection, owned JSON values and typed syscall arguments and results. Keep ordinary serialized syscalls when capabilities are absent and preserve value ownership across query, database, storage, metadata, scheduler and registration adapters. Include focused owned-value regressions.

Transfer owned index-range and search-filter arrays between consumed builder wrappers instead of copying every prefix. Preserve value capture timing and reject reentrant or repeated use, including after capture throws.
